      "notice": "Look at the left-hand side of 钱. That is 钅 — 金 squeezed thin. The character carries metal inside it.",
      "discover": "For most of Chinese history money WAS metal: bronze coins, cast with a square hole so they could be strung together and carried in the thousands. A character for money built out of the character for metal is not a coincidence — it is a description.",
